# Aquarium64 as an XScreenSaver program.
#
# XScreenSaver shows every entry of the "programs:" list of ~/.xscreensaver
# as a selectable screensaver. Add a line for Aquarium64 to that list.
# The trailing "\" continues the line, and the literal "\n\" terminates it.
#
# In ~/.xscreensaver:
#
#   programs:                                                   \
#       "Aquarium64"    /usr/bin/aquarium64 --fullscreen \n\
#
# Then restart XScreenSaver and pick it from the list:
#
#   xscreensaver-command -restart
#   xscreensaver-demo
#
# Notes:
# - XScreenSaver works on X11 sessions only (see README.md).
# - If the binary is installed in another location, adjust the path above,
#   or point the entry at: /usr/bin/env godot --path /path/to/Aquarium64